    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0642" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg630"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.91/217: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-06T09:00:00+03:25">May 6, 1940—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 6—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. My 91, April 30,4 p.m.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d550-f1"/> It now seems
                    practically certain that the Iranian Government has been obliged to put several
                    flying fields at the disposal of the Soviets. A number of Iranian refugees who
                    were expelled from Russia—see my despatch No. 1294, May 13, 1938<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d550-f2"/>—have just been engaged by the Iranian Air Force
                    presumably to serve as interpreters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
